# T-1085: Unqualified constructor pattern tag 'Shape' in match arm position.
# After B-344 populates tycon_env for nested dicts, the elaborate_pattern
# pass can find Shape in tycon_env and emits T018 "unqualified constructor pattern tag".
# Note: T018 fires when the PATTERN TAG is the type name (Shape), not a constructor name
# (Circle, Square). Constructor names are not in tycon_env; only the TyCon name is.
[
  Shape: [type [Circle radius: Int] [Square side: Int]]
  v: [Circle radius: 5]
  result: [match v
    [Shape _]: -1
    _: 99]
]
=== out
Dict({"Circle": Function(payload), "Square": Function(payload), "v": Variant(Shape.Circle, Dict({"radius": Int(5)})), "result": Int(99)})

=== warn
unqualified constructor pattern tag 'Shape'
